  "worked_solution": "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field with simply connected domain $D\u2286{R}^{2},$ then the following are equivalent:\n\n- $F$ is a source-free vector field.\n\n- $\u2207\\cdot F=\\frac{\u2202P}{\u2202x}+\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202y}=0.$\n\n- The flux ${\u222e}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s$ along any closed curve $C\u2282D$ is zero.\n\n- Flux is path-independent. That is, given any two curves ${C}_{1},{C}_{2}\u2282D$ with the same start and endpoints, we have that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\n- There exists a stream function $\u03c8(x,y)$ for $F.$\n\nNote that $F(x,y)=-{x}^{2}{e}^{-y}\\,i-2x{e}^{-y}\\,j$ is a vector field with the simply connected domain $D={R}^{2},$ where $P(x,y)=-{x}^{2}{e}^{-y}$ and $Q(x,y)=-2x{e}^{-y}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\u2202P}{\u2202x}=-2x{e}^{-y},\\,\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202y} & =2x{e}^{-y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, we have that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\u2202P}{\u2202x}+\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202y}=-2x{e}^{-y}+2x{e}^{-y}=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. This follows from statement I.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $F$ is source-free, the result ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s=0$ is guaranteed for closed curves only.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"",
